          "text": "On admission (Day 1) she had a BP of 148/86 mmHg, HR 92, and oxygen saturations of 94% on room air. ECG showed T-wave inversion in V4-6, and troponin rose from 287 to 412. GRACE score was high risk. Inpatient angiogram demonstrated severe three-vessel coronary artery disease; following MDT review, PCI was not pursued and a decision was made for medical management. Renal function was monitored in the context of contrast use, with creatinine 168 on Day 2 improving to 142 by Day 4. Treatment included commencement of ticagrelor (dual antiplatelet therapy) and fondaparinux, uptitration of bisoprolol to 7.5mg once daily, and addition of isosorbide mononitrate 30mg once daily. She mobilised with physiotherapy and a cardiac rehabilitation referral was completed.",
